  # Shai-Hulud Sentinel Rule
  
  *Detection rule · `rule::1.0` · version 1 · modified 2026-01-02 · TLP:CLEAR*
  
  Detects suspicious cloud data gathering sequences tied to the Shai-Hulud objective.
  
  | Property | Value |
  | --- | --- |
  | Severity | High |
  | Detection model | [Shai-Hulud Objective](../objectives/shai-hulud-objective.md) |
  | ATT&CK | [`T1589`](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1589) Gather Victim Identity Information |
  | Platforms | Microsoft Sentinel: `STAGING` (PREVIEW runs) |
  | Playbook | PB-IR-001 |
  | Responders | soc_l1 |
  
  **On this page:** [Deployment](#deployment) · [Platform configuration](#platform-configuration) · [Response](#response) · [ATT&CK techniques](#attck-techniques) · [Detection coverage](#detection-coverage) · [Metadata](#metadata)
  
  ## Deployment
  
  What `opentide deploy` does with this rule: each platform block's status, the runs that act on it, and the tenants they reach.
  
  | Platform | Status | Deployed by | Tenants | Block enabled |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | Microsoft Sentinel | `STAGING` | PREVIEW runs | `staging` | yes |
  
  - `STAGING` (strategy `PREVIEW`): Under test on the staging tenant
  
